---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import StatusDashboard from '../components/StatusDashboard.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';

const clientUrl = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_CLIENT_URL || 'http://localhost:8787/client/';
const clientScreenshot = withBase('images/client-screenshot.png');
---

<Layout title="Home" description="SpaceAge - Open PBEM Campaign Lobby">
  <section class="hero">
	<div class="hero-content">
	  <h1>SpaceAge Campaign</h1>
	  <p class="tagline">An Open Play-by-Email Galactic Strategy Game</p>

	  <p class="closed-lobby">
		This campaign is <strong>invitation-only</strong> — a closed table for ten player factions.
		There is no public sign-up; this site is for players and observers of that table.
	  </p>

	  <div class="attribution-block card" id="attribution">
		<h2>Lineage &amp; Attribution</h2>
		<p>
		  Original ideas are taken from <strong>Lorelei</strong>,
		  <strong><a href="https://github.com/pbem-games/Atlantis" rel="noopener noreferrer">Atlantis</a></strong>,
		  <strong>Eressea</strong>, <strong>Rise of Heroes</strong> and <strong>Alderson games</strong>
		  and influenced by <strong>Jiří Klouda</strong>, <strong>Vincent Archer</strong>,
		  <strong>Joseph Traub</strong> and other authors. <strong>Archer</strong> specifically wrote a 1998
		  generic PBEM engine used by Overlord and then Rise of Heroes (1999–2000), intended for
		  Alderson game that never fully blossomed. SpaceAge sits in that family a
		  <strong>spiritual successor</strong>, hopefully expanding on those games.
		</p>
		<p class="attribution-links">
		  <a href="https://github.com/pbem-games/Atlantis" rel="noopener noreferrer">Atlantis (GitHub)</a>
		  ·
		  <a href="https://github.com/pbem-games/wasteland" rel="noopener noreferrer">Wasteland (GitHub)</a>
		  ·
		  <a href="https://overlord.sourceforge.net/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Overlord PBEM engine (SourceForge)</a>
		</p>
	  </div>

	  <div class="flavour">
		<h2>The Alderson Points</h2>
		<p class="flavour-lead">
		  Our future maybe in our future, here, in the Milky Way?
		</p>
		<p>
		  <strong>Dan Alderson</strong> theorised <strong>weak points</strong> in space-time at the
		  <strong>fringes of gravity wells</strong>. From those points one could jump to another. The experimental
		  <strong>Alderson Drive</strong> in mid XXI century sent an expedition more than
		  <strong>750 light-years</strong> — and back the next week — in the wink of an eye.
		</p>
		<p>
		  It appeared that the &ldquo;Drive&rdquo; is not drive at all, it's a matter of high energy oscillation of
		  particles achievable in any fusion reactor at a very specific point in space. When that happens an oscillating
		  bubble around that point is quantum entangled to its paired point and a bubble is at the same time
		  &ldquo;here&rdquo; and &ldquo;there&rdquo; with certain probability of being at one of those points at the
		  moment of stopping the oscillation. The trick is to end it &ldquo;there&rdquo;, selecting the moment where
		  bubble is big enough that is can cover the entire ship and mathing the speeds and vectors of moving bubble
		  with a meter level granularity when the closests orientating points are millions of kilometers away.
		</p>
		<p>
		  Today those <strong>Points</strong> link the galaxy, the maths has been mastered. Resources await explorers,
		  traders, operators, and captains.
		</p>
		<p>
		  In a single catastrophic day on <strong>18 September 2152</strong>, the Points
		  <strong>shut down</strong> for no apparent reasons. <strong>Commerce died. Colonies starved.</strong>
		  After <strong>four years</strong>, most reopened, some new points appeared some pairs become unstable.
		  Some systems remain isolated. And <strong>two Points that led to Earth stayed dark</strong>, leaving only
		  mystery and <strong>Fear</strong>.
		</p>
		<p>
		  This is the story of the systems lost on the fringes of galaxy. The colonies are thriving, the
		  <strong>United Star Nation</strong> push for civilization and research that will enable the
		  <strong>Rejoin</strong>, but for now the return to <strong>Sol</strong> is not an option. As a founding
		  members of the colonies you are to decide what is next.
		</p>
	  </div>

	  <div class="pbem-intro card">
		<h3>How Play-by-Email Works</h3>
		<p>
		  You do not log into a live game. Instead, you read last quarter's report (text for now, visual tools later),
		  discuss strategy, and submit orders. When all factions are ready, the game engine processes the turn and
		  publishes new reports. The cycle repeats each quarter.
		</p>
	  </div>

	</div>

	<div class="hero-visual">
	  <a href={clientUrl} class="client-screenshot-link" aria-label="SpaceAge client">
		<img
		  src={clientScreenshot}
		  alt="SpaceAge client — star map, unit tree, and order editor"
		  width="1024"
		  height="461"
		  loading="lazy"
		/>
	  </a>
	</div>
  </section>

  <section class="dashboard-section">
	<h2>Game Status</h2>
	<StatusDashboard />
  </section>

  <section class="features-section">
	<h2>Game Features</h2>
	<div class="features-grid">
	  <div class="card">
		<h3>Quarterly Turns</h3>
		<p>Each turn represents 13 weeks of in-game time. Strategy and diplomacy unfold across months of real time.</p>
	  </div>
	  <div class="card">
		<h3>Deep Technology Tree</h3>
		<p>Research and develop technologies across 10 levels, from basic fusion drives to advanced weapons and modules.</p>
	  </div>
	  <div class="card">
		<h3>Rich Simulation</h3>
		<p>Combat mechanics, resource management, crew skills, planetary environments, and diplomacy all affect your success.</p>
	  </div>
	  <div class="card">
		<h3>Planning Tools</h3>
		<p><a href={withBase('eta')}>Transit ETA</a> calculator and <a href={withBase('battle')}>battle what-if</a> (estimates only).</p>
	  </div>
	</div>
  </section>

  <section class="rules-preview-section card">
	<h2>Quick Start</h2>
	<p>New to SpaceAge? Start with the <a href={withBase('rules')}>rules overview</a> to understand the core mechanics.</p>
	<p>Want to dive deeper? Check out the <a href={withBase('client')}>client page</a> for installation and getting started.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero {
	display: grid;
	grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
	gap: var(--space-2xl);
	margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
	align-items: center;
  }

  .hero-content {
	display: flex;
	flex-direction: column;
	gap: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .hero h1 {
	font-size: var(--font-size-3xl);
	color: var(--color-accent-teal);
	margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .tagline {
	font-size: var(--font-size-xl);
	color: var(--color-accent-amber);
	font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
  }

  .closed-lobby {
	background-color: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.12);
	border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent-amber);
	padding: var(--space-md) var(--space-lg);
	border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  }

  .attribution-block h2 {
	margin-top: 0;
	color: var(--color-accent-teal);
  }

  .flavour {
	background-color: rgba(13, 148, 136, 0.1);
	padding: var(--space-lg);
	border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent-teal);
	border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  }

  .flavour h2 {
	margin-top: 0;
	color: var(--color-accent-teal);
	font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
  }

  .flavour-lead {
	font-style: italic;
  }

  .pbem-intro {
	margin: var(--space-lg) 0;
  }

  .hero-visual {
	display: flex;
	align-items: center;
	justify-content: center;
  }

  .client-screenshot-link {
	display: block;
	border: 2px solid var(--color-accent-teal);
	border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
	overflow: hidden;
	line-height: 0;
	transition: border-color 0.15s ease, box-shadow 0.15s ease;
  }

  .client-screenshot-link:hover,
  .client-screenshot-link:focus-visible {
	border-color: var(--color-accent-amber);
	box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.25);
  }

  .client-screenshot-link img {
	display: block;
	width: 100%;
	height: auto;
  }

  .dashboard-section {
	margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .features-section {
	margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .features-grid {
	display: grid;
	grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));
	gap: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .rules-preview-section {
	margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
	.hero {
	  grid-template-columns: 1fr;
	}

  }
</style>
